SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] Earth Day: Sustainability Resources Presentation
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nHow much could you save from the 
 landfill?\n\nLEARN A NEW WAY TO RECYCLE\nPlastic bags of all sorts have 
 never been recyclable. They end up in landfills and incinerators. But now 
 there is a new way to recycle the unrecyclable. Learn how Ridwell a company 
 based in Seattle takes your bread chip and candy bags and other plastic 
 trash and sends them on to a new life possibly as decking or drainage 
 systems. Learn how you can reduce waste and repurpose plastic into 
 something useful. \n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis class is run by the MILL. 
 Please register for classes directly through their website here.\n\nFor 
 questions about MILL classes please call 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL @ MPL is 
 made possible through a partnership between the MILL\, Montclair Public 
 Library and Partners for Health.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Health & Wellness
