BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260506T223000Z
DTEND:20260506T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260506T000000Z
SUMMARY:5K Training - No Boundaries
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class.\n\nClick here to register 
 for the early bird price\, available until April 3rd.\n\nClick here for 
 registrations April 3rd and later.\n\nHave you always wanted to run or walk 
 a 5K but didn't know how to begin training? Maybe you are nervous or don't 
 want to do it alone? Maybe you have had a hard time sticking to a training 
 program in the past? If you answered "Yes" to any of the above\, our iconic 
 beginner program is perfect for you. Often the first step is the 
 hardest.\n\nThe camaraderie of a group and experience of your coaches and 
 mentors provide great support toward healthier habits and lifestyle. This 
 program is designed for people just starting a walking/running routine for 
 the first time\, restarting after a winter hiatus and those who want to run 
 faster or longer. In 8 weeks\, meeting twice a week\, our fun\, 
 unintimidating program will help you walk\, walk-run or run across the 
 finish line at the Fitzgerald 5k Lager Run in June.\n\nIn collaboration 
 with Dawn and John Fabbro of Fleet Feet Montclair.\n
LOCATION:Montclair - Anderson Park\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-15827866
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15827866
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260506T223000Z
DTEND:20260507T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260506T000000Z
SUMMARY:AI Basics in Gemini and Claude for Seasoned Professionals NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nUsing AI as a thinking partner—not a replacement for 
 expertise\n\nDesigned for experienced professionals who want to understand 
 and responsibly integrate AI into their work\, this 90-minute workshop 
 introduces the core features of Google Gemini and Anthropic’s Claude. 
 Participants will explore Gemini’s GEMs and image generation 
 capabilities\, as well as Claude’s artifacts and strengths in analyzing 
 and generating longer-form content.\n\nThe session includes practical 
 guidance on effective prompting frameworks\, multimodal workflows\, and the 
 everyday language of AI. Real-world use cases will be discussed to help 
 participants apply AI as a strategic collaborator while maintaining their 
 own voice and expertise.\n\nParticipants should bring a laptop or tablet 
 and be logged into the free versions of Gemini and Claude before class. 
 Handouts will be provided.\n\nPlease note: The Bellevue Avenue Branch is 
 NOT wheelchair accessible\n
LOCATION:Montclair Bellevue Ave Branch - First Floor\, Montclair Bellevue Avenue Branch
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Computers & Technology
