SUMMARY:A History of the Presby Iris Gardens NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School class. Click below to 
 register.\n\nOften called "the rainbow on the hill\," Montclair's famous 
 Presby Iris Gardens contain over 14\,000 irises of approximately 3\,000 
 varieties from all over the world and produce over 100\,000 blooms over the 
 course of the season. The Gardens were started in the 1920s as a memorial 
 to Frank H. Presby\, one of the founders of the American Iris Society and a 
 Montclair local. Learn how the history of the Gardens at Presby entwines 
 with the history of Montclair\, its active citizens\, and its early 
 cultural scene. May is the perfect time of year to learn more about this 
 unique park and to visit the irises in bloom.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-16322289
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16322289
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260512T150000Z
DTEND:20260512T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T000000Z
SUMMARY:Understanding Medicare
DESCRIPTION:Confused about Medicare? Join us for an informative session 
 that breaks down the basics of this federal health insurance program. Learn 
 who qualifies\, including adults age 65 and older\, younger individuals 
 with disabilities\, and those with End-Stage Renal Disease 
 (ESRD).\n\nWe’ll explain the different parts of Medicare—Part A 
 (hospital insurance)\, Part B (medical insurance)\, and Part D 
 (prescription drug coverage)—and what services each covers. The program 
 will also explore your coverage options\, including Original Medicare with 
 supplemental (Medigap) plans and Medicare Advantage (Part C).\n\nThis 
 session is ideal for anyone approaching Medicare eligibility\, caregivers\, 
 or those looking to better understand their health coverage 
 choices.\n\nPresented by Medicare Specialist Jacki Spear.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Classroom
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services
UID:LibCal-10306-16592247
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16592247
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260512T171500Z
DTEND:20260512T181500Z
DTSTAMP:20260512T000000Z
SUMMARY:Everything Book Club\, "A Rising Man" by Abir Mukherjee
DESCRIPTION:Winner of CWA Dagger Award. A richly atmospheric\, twisting 
 "mystorical" set in Calcutta\, 1919. The body of a senior official has been 
 found in a filthy sewer\, and a note left in his mouth warns the British to 
 quit India\, or else. Captain Sam Wyndham\, former Scotland Yard 
 detective\, and Sergeant Banerjee\, one of the few Indians to be recruited 
 into the new CID—embark on an investigation that will take them from the 
 mansions of British traders to the opium dens of the city. Perfect for AAPI 
 Heritage Month! \n\n“An enthralling debut.”—The New York 
 Times\n\nAbir Mukherjee is the child of immigrants from India who grew up 
 in Scotland. After 20 years of working as an accounted\, he started writing 
 crime fiction. "A Rising Man" is his debut novel. Mukherjee lives near 
 London. \n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-15933640
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15933640
END:VEVENT
